  - elementId: metric-notes
    elementType: text
    bounds: [48, 424, 864, 53]
    content:
      fontSize: 13
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p><strong>Reading:</strong> lower log loss, Brier loss, and ECE are better; higher top-one strike and AUC are better. Runner AUC is descriptive because runners within a race are dependent.</p>
        <p>Uniform ECE is degenerate under tied runner-level bins and should not be read as evidence of useful calibration.</p>
